{"id":"mahabharata-3-204","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":204,"title":"चतुरधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 204 · The hunter's aged parents","summary":{"en":"Delighted by the teaching, Kaushika honours the hunter, who leads him into his house and shows him his aged father and mother, whom he serves as his gods. The old couple bless the Brahmin, and the hunter explains that this service is the source of his wisdom.","kn":"ಉಪದೇಶದಿಂದ ಸಂತೋಷಗೊಂಡ ಕೌಶಿಕನು ವ್ಯಾಧನನ್ನು ಗೌರವಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವ್ಯಾಧನು ಅವನನ್ನು ಮನೆಯೊಳಗೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ದು ತಾನು ದೇವರಂತೆ ಸೇವಿಸುವ ವೃದ್ಧ ತಂದೆತಾಯಿಯರನ್ನು ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವೃದ್ಧದಂಪತಿಗಳು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನನ್ನು ಆಶೀರ್ವದಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಈ ಸೇವೆಯೇ ತನ್ನ ಜ್ಞಾನದ ಮೂಲವೆಂದು ವ್ಯಾಧನು ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"उपदेश से प्रसन्न कौशिक व्याध का सम्मान करते हैं, जो उन्हें घर के भीतर ले जाकर अपने वृद्ध माता-पिता दिखाता है, जिनकी वह देवताओं की तरह सेवा करता है। वृद्ध दम्पती ब्राह्मण को आशीर्वाद देते हैं, और व्याध बताता है कि यही सेवा उसके ज्ञान का स्रोत है।","te":"ఉపదేశంతో సంతోషించిన కౌశికుడు వ్యాధుని గౌరవిస్తాడు; వ్యాధుడు అతనిని ఇంట్లోకి తీసుకువెళ్లి తాను దేవుళ్లలా సేవించే వృద్ధ తల్లిదండ్రులను చూపిస్తాడు. వృద్ధ దంపతులు బ్రాహ్మణుని ఆశీర్వదిస్తారు; ఈ సేవే తన జ్ఞానానికి మూలమని వ్యాధుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"உபதேசத்தால் மகிழ்ந்த கௌஶிகர் வ்யாதனைக் கௌரவிக்க, அவன் அவரை வீட்டுக்குள் அழைத்துச் சென்று தான் தெய்வங்களாகப் பேணும் முதிய தாய் தந்தையரைக் காட்டுகிறான். முதிய தம்பதியர் அந்தணரை ஆசீர்வதிக்க, இந்தப் பணிவிடையே தன் ஞானத்தின் ஊற்று என்று வ்யாதன் விளக்குகிறான்.","ml":"ഈ ഉപദേശത്തിൽ സന്തോഷിച്ച കൗശികൻ വ്യാധനെ ബഹുമാനിക്കുന്നു; വ്യാധൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വീട്ടിലേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോയി വൃദ്ധരായ അച്ഛനെയും അമ്മയെയും കാണിക്കുന്നു; അവരെ ദേവതകളെപ്പോലെ അദ്ദേഹം സേവിക്കുന്നു. വൃദ്ധദമ്പതികൾ ബ്രാഹ്മണനെ അനുഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നു; ഈ സേവനമാണ് തന്റെ ജ്ഞാനത്തിന്റെ ഉറവിടമെന്ന് വ്യാധൻ വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.204; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं संकथिते कृत्स्ने मोक्षधर्मे युधिष्ठिर ।\nदृढं प्रीतमना विप्रो धर्मव्याधमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the whole dharma of liberation had been told thus, Yudhishthira, the brahmin, greatly pleased in mind, said to the dharma-hunter:"}},{"n":2,"text":"न्याययुक्तमिदं सर्वं भवता परिकीर्तितम् ।\nन तेऽस्त्यविदितं किंचिद्धर्मेष्विह हि दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this that you have declared is in accord with right; nothing seems unknown to you about dharma here."}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रत्यक्षं मम यो धर्मस्तं पश्य द्विजसत्तम ।\nयेन सिद्धिरियं प्राप्ता मया ब्राह्मणपुंगव ॥","meaning":{"en":"See, best of brahmins, the dharma that is before my eyes, by which I have attained this success, bull among brahmins."}},{"n":4,"text":"उत्तिष्ठ भगवन्क्षिप्रं प्रविश्याभ्यन्तरं गृहम् ।\nद्रष्टुमर्हसि धर्मज्ञ मातरं पितरं च मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rise, revered one, quickly, and enter the inner house. You ought to see my mother and my father, knower of dharma."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"इत्युक्तः स प्रविश्याथ ददर्श परमार्चितम् ।\nसौधं हृद्यं चतुःशालमतीव च मनोहरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so, he entered and saw a lovely, much honoured four-halled mansion, most charming,"}},{"n":6,"text":"देवतागृहसंकाशं दैवतैश्च सुपूजितम् ।\nशयनासनसंबाधं गन्धैश्च परमैर्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"like a temple of the gods and well worshipped with divine images, crowded with beds and seats and filled with excellent perfumes."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्र शुक्लाम्बरधरौ पितरावस्य पूजितौ ।\nकृताहारौ सुतुष्टौ तावुपविष्टौ वरासने ।\nधर्मव्याधस्तु तौ दृष्ट्वा पादेषु शिरसापतत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw the hunter's parents, honoured, dressed in white, who had eaten and were quite content, seated on fine seats; and the dharma-hunter, seeing them, fell with his head at their feet."}},{"text":"वृद्धावूचतुः","meaning":{"en":"The two elders said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"उत्तिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ धर्मज्ञ धर्मस्त्वामभिरक्षतु ।\nप्रीतौ स्वस्तव शौचेन दीर्घमायुरवाप्नुहि ।\nसत्पुत्रेण त्वया पुत्र नित्यकालं सुपूजितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rise, rise, knower of dharma; may dharma protect you. We are pleased with your purity; gain long life. By you, our good son, we are always well honoured."}},{"n":9,"text":"न तेऽन्यद्दैवतं किंचिद्दैवतेष्वपि वर्तते ।\nप्रयतत्वाद्द्विजातीनां दमेनासि समन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have no other god among the gods; through your purity toward the twice-born you are endowed with self-control."}},{"n":10,"text":"पितुः पितामहा ये च तथैव प्रपितामहाः ।\nप्रीतास्ते सततं पुत्र दमेनावां च पूजया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father's father and grandfather, and likewise great-grandfathers, are always pleased, son, by your self-control and by your worship of us."}},{"n":11,"text":"मनसा कर्मणा वाचा शुश्रूषा नैव हीयते ।\nन चान्या वितथा बुद्धिर्दृश्यते सांप्रतं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"In mind, deed and speech your service never fails, and no other false intent is seen in you now."}},{"n":12,"text":"जामदग्न्येन रामेण यथा वृद्धौ सुपूजितौ ।\nतथा त्वया कृतं सर्वं तद्विशिष्टं च पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Rama, son of Jamadagni, honoured his aged parents well, so have you done all, and better, my son."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"ततस्तं ब्राह्मणं ताभ्यां धर्मव्याधो न्यवेदयत् ।\nतौ स्वागतेन तं विप्रमर्चयामासतुस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the dharma-hunter presented that brahmin to them, and they honoured the brahmin with a welcome."}},{"n":14,"text":"प्रतिगृह्य च तां पूजां द्विजः पप्रच्छ तावुभौ ।\nसपुत्राभ्यां सभृत्याभ्यां कच्चिद्वां कुशलं गृहे ।\nअनामयं च वां कच्चित्सदैवेह शरीरयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Accepting that honour, the brahmin asked them both, \"Is all well in your house with you, with your son and servants? Are your bodies always free from illness?\""}},{"text":"वृद्धावूचतुः","meaning":{"en":"The two elders said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"कुशलं नो गृहे विप्र भृत्यवर्गे च सर्वशः ।\nकच्चित्त्वमप्यविघ्नेन संप्राप्तो भगवन्निह ॥","meaning":{"en":"All is well in our house, brahmin, and with all our servants; and have you, revered one, arrived here without trouble?"}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"बाढमित्येव तौ विप्रः प्रत्युवाच मुदान्वितः ।\nधर्मव्याधस्तु तं विप्रमर्थवद्वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yes,\" the brahmin replied to them, delighted. And the dharma-hunter then spoke meaningful words to the brahmin."}},{"n":17,"text":"पिता माता च भगवन्नेतौ मे दैवतं परम् ।\nयद्दैवतेभ्यः कर्तव्यं तदेताभ्यां करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Revered one, this father and mother are my highest god. What is to be done for the gods I do for these two."}},{"n":18,"text":"त्रयस्त्रिंशद्यथा देवाः सर्वे शक्रपुरोगमाः ।\nसंपूज्याः सर्वलोकस्य तथा वृद्धाविमौ मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the thirty-three gods, led by Indra, are to be worshipped by all the world, so are these two aged ones for me."}},{"n":19,"text":"उपहारानाहरन्तो देवतानां यथा द्विजाः ।\nकुर्वते तद्वदेताभ्यां करोम्यहमतन्द्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As brahmins bring offerings to the gods, so I unwearied do for these two."}},{"n":20,"text":"एतौ मे परमं ब्रह्मन्पिता माता च दैवतम् ।\nएतौ पुष्पैः फलै रत्नैस्तोषयामि सदा द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two, brahmin, are my highest, father and mother, and my god. I always please them with flowers, fruits and gems, brahmin."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतावेवाग्नयो मह्यं यान्वदन्ति मनीषिणः ।\nयज्ञा वेदाश्च चत्वारः सर्वमेतौ मम द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two are my fires, those the wise speak of; they are my sacrifices and the four Vedas, they are everything to me, brahmin."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतदर्थं मम प्राणा भार्या पुत्राः सुहृज्जनाः ।\nसपुत्रदारः शुश्रूषां नित्यमेव करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason my life, wife, sons and friends exist; with my sons and wife I always serve them."}},{"n":23,"text":"स्वयं च स्नापयाम्येतौ तथा पादौ प्रधावये ।\nआहारं संप्रयच्छामि स्वयं च द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I bathe them myself and wash their feet, and I give them food myself, best of brahmins."}},{"n":24,"text":"अनुकूलाः कथा वच्मि विप्रियं परिवर्जयन् ।\nअधर्मेणापि संयुक्तं प्रियमाभ्यां करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I speak agreeable words, avoiding what is unpleasing, and I do what pleases them even if it is joined with unrighteousness."}},{"n":25,"text":"धर्ममेव गुरुं ज्ञात्वा करोमि द्विजसत्तम ।\nअतन्द्रितः सदा विप्र शुश्रूषां वै करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing dharma itself to be the teacher, I do this, best of brahmins; unwearied, I always serve them."}},{"n":26,"text":"पञ्चैव गुरवो ब्रह्मन्पुरुषस्य बुभूषतः ।\nपिता माताग्निरात्मा च गुरुश्च द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are five teachers, brahmin, for a man who wishes to prosper: father, mother, fire, the self and the teacher, best of brahmins."}},{"n":27,"text":"एतेषु यस्तु वर्तेत सम्यगेव द्विजोत्तम ।\nभवेयुरग्नयस्तस्य परिचीर्णास्तु नित्यशः ।\nगार्हस्थ्ये वर्तमानस्य धर्म एष सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who deals rightly with these, best of brahmins, has his fires always tended; this is the eternal dharma for one living as a householder."}}]}]}